      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the bit about \"double effect\" is helpful, but i feel like the liberal side is being presented with a lot of nuanced ethical frameworks while the conservative side still feels a bit one-dimensional, like it's just about following rules. \n\ncould you provide a more rigorous philosophical breakdown for the conservative position? specifically, how do they address the tension between the \"divine gift\" argument and the concept of human stewardship or the duty to alleviate suffering? i want to make sure i'm not just portraying them as being \"anti-autonomy\" without understanding the actual ethical weight of their position.",
